---
import * as stylex from "@stylexjs/stylex"
import { styles } from "../components/landing/LandingStyles.js"
import "../components/docs/JobVisual.css";
import System from "../components/landing/System.astro";
import "../components/landing/Landing.css";
import "../styles/site/tokens.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Effect-native durable jobs. Schema-defined work, atomic PostgreSQL enqueue, and explicit scoped workers."
    />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#090b10" />
    <title>effect-jobs — Give background work a durable home</title>
  </head>
  <body class:list={["ej-landing", stylex.attrs(styles.element7).class]}>
    <a class:list={["skip", stylex.attrs(styles.element8).class]} href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class:list={["site-header wrap", stylex.attrs(styles.wrap).class]}>
      <a class:list={["wordmark", stylex.attrs(styles.element9).class]} href="/" aria-label="effect-jobs home"
        ><span class:list={["mark", stylex.attrs(styles.mark).class]} aria-hidden="true">e<span {...stylex.attrs(styles.workerPairSelected)}>j</span></span
        >effect-jobs</a
      >
      <nav {...stylex.attrs(styles.element10)} aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a {...stylex.attrs(styles.element11)} href="/docs">Documentation</a><a {...stylex.attrs(styles.element11)} href="/demo"
          >Demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </nav>
      <span class:list={["alpha", stylex.attrs(styles.alpha).class]}>PUBLIC ALPHA</span>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class:list={["hero wrap", stylex.attrs(styles.hero).class]} aria-labelledby="promise">
        <div class:list={["eyebrow", stylex.attrs(styles.eyebrow).class]}>
          <span class:list={["tiny-mark", stylex.attrs(styles.tinyMark).class]} aria-hidden="true"></span> DURABLE EXECUTION ·
          NATIVE EFFECT
        </div>
        <h1 {...stylex.attrs(styles.element12)} id="promise">
          Your request ends.<br /><span {...stylex.attrs(styles.workerPairSelected)}>The work goes on.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class:list={["hero-copy", stylex.attrs(styles.heroCopy).class]}>
          Give background work a durable home. Schema-defined jobs, atomic
          PostgreSQL enqueue, and scoped workers that compose with your Effect
          application.
        </p>
        <div class:list={["actions", stylex.attrs(styles.actions).class]}>
          <a class:list={["primary", stylex.attrs(styles.element13).class]} href="/docs/start/first-job"
            >Build your first job <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          ><a class:list={["secondary", stylex.attrs(styles.element14).class]} href="/demo"
            >Explore the demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
        <p class:list={["hero-note", stylex.attrs(styles.heroNote).class]}>
          Your database. Your transactions. Explicit execution.
        </p>
        <System />
      </section>
      <section class:list={["stack-strip wrap", stylex.attrs(styles.wrap2).class]} aria-label="Supported stack">
        <span {...stylex.attrs(styles.stackStrip)}>BUILT TO COMPOSE</span><strong {...stylex.attrs(styles.stackStrip2)}>Effect 4.0.5</strong><i {...stylex.attrs(styles.stackStrip3)}
          aria-hidden="true">/</i
        ><strong {...stylex.attrs(styles.stackStrip2)}>PostgreSQL</strong><i {...stylex.attrs(styles.stackStrip3)} aria-hidden="true">/</i><strong {...stylex.attrs(styles.stackStrip2)}
          >Node.js · Bun</strong
        ><i {...stylex.attrs(styles.stackStrip3)} aria-hidden="true">/</i><strong {...stylex.attrs(styles.stackStrip2)}>Optional Drizzle</strong>
      </section>
      <section class:list={["atomic wrap section", stylex.attrs(styles.atomic).class]} aria-labelledby="atomic-title">
        <div>
          <p class:list={["eyebrow", stylex.attrs(styles.eyebrow2).class]}>01 / CLOSE THE GAP</p><h2 {...stylex.attrs(styles.element15)} id="atomic-title">
            The write and the work.<br /><span {...stylex.attrs(styles.systemSubtitle)}>One transaction.</span>
          </h2><p {...stylex.attrs(styles.eyebrow3)}>
            A report request is only useful if its job exists too. Join
            application writes and enqueue in the same configured client
            transaction: commit together, or roll back together.
          </p><a class:list={["text-link", stylex.attrs(styles.element16).class]} href="/docs/persistence/transactions"
            >Understand atomic enqueue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          >
        </div>
        <div class:list={["transaction-card", stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard).class]}>
          <div class:list={["panel-label", stylex.attrs(styles.panelLabel).class]}>
            <span>TRANSACTION BOUNDARY</span><span class:list={["status-dot", stylex.attrs(styles.statusDot).class]}
              >same client</span
            >
          </div><ol {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard2)}>
            <li {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard3)}>
              <span {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard4)}>01</span><div>
                <strong {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard5)}>Save report request</strong><small {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard6)}
                  >Application-owned business data</small
                >
              </div>
            </li><li {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard3)}>
              <span {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard4)}>02</span><div>
                <strong {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard5)}>Enqueue report job</strong><small {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard6)}
                  >Producer identity + encoded payload</small
                >
              </div>
            </li><li {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard3)}>
              <span {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard4)}>03</span><div>
                <strong {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard5)}>Commit together</strong><small {...stylex.attrs(styles.transactionCard6)}
                  >Joined enqueue results are provisional until commit</small
                >
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol><div class:list={["identity", stylex.attrs(styles.identity).class]}>
            <span {...stylex.attrs(styles.identity2)}>REPEATED REQUEST?</span><p {...stylex.attrs(styles.eyebrow4)}>
              The same <code {...stylex.attrs(styles.element4)}>(operation, operationId, slot)</code> and matching semantics
              find the retained job. Changed semantics produce a conflict.
            </p><a {...stylex.attrs(styles.element17)} href="/docs/persistence/deduplication"
              >How deduplication works →</a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section
        class:list={["wrap section reliability", stylex.attrs(styles.wrap3).class]}
        aria-labelledby="reliability-title"
      >
        <p class:list={["eyebrow", stylex.attrs(styles.eyebrow2).class]}>02 / MAKE FAILURE EXPLICIT</p><div
          class:list={["section-heading", stylex.attrs(styles.sectionHeading).class]}
        >
          <h2 {...stylex.attrs(styles.element15)} id="reliability-title">
            Reliability has<br /><span {...stylex.attrs(styles.systemSubtitle)}>more than one path.</span>
          </h2><p {...stylex.attrs(styles.eyebrow5)}>
            Retries are a policy. Ownership is a lease. An uncertain external
            outcome still needs application-level reconciliation.
          </p>
        </div><div class:list={["principles", stylex.attrs(styles.principles).class]}>
          <article {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles2)}>
            <span class:list={["principle-icon", stylex.attrs(styles.principleIcon).class]} aria-hidden="true">↻</span><h3 {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles3)}>
              Retries that persist
            </h3><p {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles4)}>
              A confirmed retry stores the next availability using the first
              persisted policy and a bounded attempt budget.
            </p><a {...stylex.attrs(styles.element18)} href="/docs/execution/retries">Retry semantics →</a>
          </article><article {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles2)}>
            <span class:list={["principle-icon", stylex.attrs(styles.principleIcon).class]} aria-hidden="true">⌁</span><h3 {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles3)}>
              Ownership that fences
            </h3><p {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles4)}>
              Database-time leases and exact ownership checks guard durable
              finalization. External side effects still need idempotency.
            </p><a {...stylex.attrs(styles.element18)} href="/docs/execution/recovery">Leases & recovery →</a>
          </article><article {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles2)}>
            <span class:list={["principle-icon", stylex.attrs(styles.principleIcon).class]} aria-hidden="true">?</span><h3 {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles3)}>
              Unknown stays unknown
            </h3><p {...stylex.attrs(styles.principles4)}>
              A lost response does not prove rollback. OutcomeUnknown is an
              attempt outcome, not a durable job state or permission to replay.
            </p><a {...stylex.attrs(styles.element18)} href="/docs/concepts/lifecycle">Follow the lifecycle →</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class:list={["wrap section finish", stylex.attrs(styles.wrap4).class]}>
        <div>
          <p class:list={["eyebrow", stylex.attrs(styles.eyebrow2).class]}>SMALL CORE. EXPLICIT BOUNDARIES.</p><h2 {...stylex.attrs(styles.element15)}>
            Make the next request<br /><span {...stylex.attrs(styles.systemSubtitle)}
              >the start of something durable.</span
            >
          </h2><p {...stylex.attrs(styles.eyebrow3)}>
            Current alpha: PostgreSQL persistence, application-owned migrations
            and pools, explicit worker lifetime. Read the supported setup before
            integrating.
          </p>
        </div><a class:list={["primary", stylex.attrs(styles.element19).class]} href="/docs/start/installation"
          >Read the installation guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class:list={["wrap", stylex.attrs(styles.wrap5).class]}>
      <a class:list={["wordmark", stylex.attrs(styles.element9).class]} href="/">effect-jobs</a><p {...stylex.attrs(styles.element20)}>
        Durable jobs, composed with Effect.
      </p><a {...stylex.attrs(styles.element21)} href="/docs">Documentation →</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
